# ========================
# Ingestion data
# ========================
# Canonical records are derived: `npm run ingest -- adapt` rebuilds them from a frozen
# snapshot in under a second and with no network traffic, so they are not worth versioning.
backend/data/canonical/

# Frozen snapshots are deliberately NOT ignored. They are the reproducibility anchor the
# methodology rests on — the raw evidence of what a source returned at a point in time, which
# cannot be regenerated once the source moves on. ~5MB per Stage 1 run; if that becomes
# unwieldy, move them to storage that versions large files rather than dropping them.
